      "id": "seg:code:overview:0013:0001",
      "blockId": "code:overview:0013",
      "type": "preserve",
      "source": "```swift\nstruct MyView: View {\n    @ObservedObject var model: DataModel\n    @Environment(\\.scenePhase) private var scenePhase\n\n    var body: some View {\n        TimerView()\n            .onChange(of: scenePhase) {\n                model.isTimerRunning = (scenePhase == .active)\n            }\n    }\n}\n```",
      "normalizedSource": "```swift struct MyView: View { @ObservedObject var model: DataModel @Environment(\\.scenePhase) private var scenePhase var body: some View { TimerView() .onChange(of: scenePhase) { model.isTimerRunning = (scenePhase == .active) } } } ```",
      "sourceHash": "5540e4fbcb1b785c1ef4342fb0bda7febbce409f494e3c3691df63a3dabf153d",
      "translatable": false,
      "preserveReason": "code",
      "contextBefore": "The following example uses the [`onChange(of:initial:_:)`](view/onchange(of:initial:_:)-8wgw9.md) method to enable a timer whenever the enclosing scene enters the [`ScenePhase.active`](scenephase/active.md) phase and disable the timer when entering any other phase:",
